Package: epicurves
Title: Gaussian-Approximated SIRD Inference and Piecewise Ensemble Growth Models for Epidemic Curves
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Raydonal", "Ospina", , "raydonal@castlab.org", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Jaciele", "Oliveira", , "jaciele.jesus@ufpe.br", role = "aut"),
    person("Cristiano", "Ferraz", , "cferraz@castlab.org", role = "aut")
    )
Description: Reference implementation accompanying two companion manuscripts
    derived from Oliveira's doctoral thesis on COVID-19 epidemic curve
    modelling. SIRD-GA is a stochastic SIRD model estimated via a
    Gaussian-diffusion approximation of the underlying density-dependent
    Markov jump process, with maximum-likelihood estimation through a
    Kalman filter under partial observation and under-reporting. The
    piecewise ensemble module combines Logistic, Gompertz and Richards
    growth curves with weights based on mean squared error or AIC, and
    identifies structural change points ("partition points") in epidemic
    growth via sequential grid search. The package reproduces every
    simulation study, table and figure reported in the two manuscripts.
